   "newText": "Preserve panel orientation and alignment; remove separator from output. Do not output the union or the holes.\n\n## ARC tiled marker extraction\nWhen an ARC grid has equal dimensions divisible by 3 and is filled with mostly 0/5 noise, with isolated marker cells in other colors, partition into 3x3 blocks. Output one cell per block, preserving the non-0/non-5 marker color at its corresponding block coordinate; output 0 for blocks without a marker. Demonstration evidence: an 18x18 input yielded a 6x6 output with markers 7, 4, 9, and 4 placed at the block coordinates containing them. A 15x15 test likewise mapped to 5x5 and was solved by this rule, with 9/8/4 markers. Ignore 0 and 5 as background/noise; do not treat them as markers. Output dimensions are input dimensions divided by 3."
